4005 0 obj
<</Title(02 - The Biggest Losses Start at the Top)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/First 4006 0 R/Last 4007 0 R/Count -2/Prev 4001 0 R/Parent 3999 0 R/Next 4008 0 R>>
endobj

4006 0 obj
<</Title(Fraud by senior leaders is rare but devastating. Authority lets them override controls, steer narratives, and hide losses inside reported numbers. Junior employees steal cash; executives rewrite results.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4005 0 R/Next 4007 0 R>>
endobj

4007 0 obj
<</Title(ACFE 2026 Report to the Nations: Owners and executives caused a median loss of $475,000, over nine times the $50,000 for staff. Financial statement fraud: 6% of cases; median loss of $ 1 million.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4006 0 R/Parent 4005 0 R>>
endobj

4008 0 obj
<</Title(03 - Weak Controls Cause Most Frauds)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/First 4009 0 R/Last 4010 0 R/Count -2/Prev 4005 0 R/Parent 3999 0 R>>
endobj

4009 0 obj
<</Title(Fraud usually succeeds because a door was left open. Missing controls, overridden approvals, and skipped reviews give opportunity room to grow. For auditors, control design is the first line of fraud prevention, and testing whether controls operate matters more than documenting that they exist.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4008 0 R/Next 4010 0 R>>
endobj

4010 0 obj
<</Title(ACFE 2026 Report to the Nations: Lack of internal controls \(33%\), management override \(19%\), and missing management review \(18%\) together drove 70% of the 2,402 cases studied across 143 countries.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4009 0 R/Parent 4008 0 R>>
endobj

