4136 0 obj
<</Title(CASE AT A GLANCE)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/First 4137 0 R/Last 4150 0 R/Count -7/Prev 4098 0 R/Parent 3931 0 R/Next 4156 0 R>>
endobj

4137 0 obj
<</Title(Organisation: Telekom Malaysia Berhad and its U.S. subsidiary, Telekom Malaysia \(USA\) Inc. Public announcement: 19 May 2026)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4136 0 R/Next 4138 0 R>>
endobj

4138 0 obj
<</Title(Period covered by the allegations: July 2020\205February 2026)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4137 0 R/Parent 4136 0 R/Next 4139 0 R>>
endobj

4139 0 obj
<</Title(Amount involved: More than US$20 million allegedly diverted)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4138 0 R/Parent 4136 0 R/Next 4140 0 R>>
endobj

4140 0 obj
<</Title(Central Themes: Corporate fraud, procurement, payroll, fabricated records and AI-assisted impersonation)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4139 0 R/Parent 4136 0 R/Next 4141 0 R>>
endobj

4141 0 obj
<</Title(The Photograph That Didn't Match the Date)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/First 4142 0 R/Last 4144 0 R/Count -3/Prev 4140 0 R/Parent 4136 0 R/Next 4145 0 R>>
endobj

4142 0 obj
<</Title(In January 2026, according to the U.S. Department of Justice \(DOJ\), the defendants sought reimbursement for expenses associated with a supposed work trip to Las Vegas in December 2025. The DOJ alleges that no such trip had taken place.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4141 0 R/Next 4143 0 R>>
endobj

4143 0 obj
<</Title(When the parent company requested photographs, the defendants allegedly arranged a later trip to Las Vegas and photographed scenes with Christmas trees to make the images appear as though they had been taken in December.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4142 0 R/Parent 4141 0 R/Next 4144 0 R>>
endobj

4144 0 obj
<</Title(The detail is striking, but the underlying issue is serious: supporting evidence can appear convincing without proving that the activity it represents actually occurred.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4143 0 R/Parent 4141 0 R>>
endobj

4145 0 obj
<</Title(The Setting)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/First 4146 0 R/Last 4149 0 R/Count -4/Prev 4141 0 R/Parent 4136 0 R/Next 4150 0 R>>
endobj

4146 0 obj
<</Title(A subsidiary sits far from head office. The parent in Malaysia relied on reports, approvals, and paperwork from the US team, and the three managers held senior positions there from July 2020 to February 2026.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4145 0 R/Next 4147 0 R>>
endobj

4147 0 obj
<</Title(At a distance, trust travels by document: a signature, an invoice, an HR record, a photograph. As the DOJ describes it, each alleged scheme aimed at one of those documents.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4146 0 R/Parent 4145 0 R/Next 4148 0 R>>
endobj

4148 0 obj
<</Title(This is why the case is useful to study. Many organisations run on the same arrangement: a head office, a remote unit and a stream of paperwork between them. The question for an auditor is simple. If the paperwork were wrong, which control would notice?)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4147 0 R/Parent 4145 0 R/Next 4149 0 R>>
endobj

4149 0 obj
<</Title(The case is particularly relevant to audit and fraud investigation professionals because the alleged schemes touched several business functions. Rather than relying on one type of transaction, the alleged conduct involved commercial contracts, procurement, human resources and employee expenses.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4148 0 R/Parent 4145 0 R>>
endobj

4150 0 obj
<</Title(Four Alleged Schemes, One Investigation)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/First 4151 0 R/Last 4155 0 R/Count -5/Prev 4145 0 R/Parent 4136 0 R>>
endobj

4151 0 obj
<</Title(1. Broadband-Capacity Sales: Selling network capacity without the required parent-company authorisation and diverting proceeds.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4150 0 R/Next 4152 0 R>>
endobj

4152 0 obj
<</Title(2. Supplier Impersonation: Misrepresenting equipment costs and directing funds to a company resembling a genuine supplier.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4151 0 R/Parent 4150 0 R/Next 4153 0 R>>
endobj

4153 0 obj
<</Title(3. Payroll Diversion: Diverting salaries belonging to former employees or interns, including through impersonation.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4152 0 R/Parent 4150 0 R/Next 4154 0 R>>
endobj

4154 0 obj
<</Title(4. Fabricated Expenses: Seeking reimbursement for a business trip that did not take place and later creating photographs to support the claim.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4153 0 R/Parent 4150 0 R/Next 4155 0 R>>
endobj

4155 0 obj
<</Title(Each alleged scheme involved a different business process, but the underlying concern was similar: information presented to the organisation did not accurately reflect the activity behind the transaction.)/Dest[38 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4154 0 R/Parent 4150 0 R>>
endobj

4156 0 obj
<</Title(HOW THE ALLEGED SCHEMES WORKED)/Dest[39 0 R/Fit]/First 4157 0 R/Last 4160 0 R/Count -4/Prev 4136 0 R/Parent 3931 0 R/Next 4161 0 R>>
endobj

4157 0 obj
<</Title(Scheme 1: Unauthorised Broadband-Capacity Sales)/Dest[39 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4156 0 R/Next 4158 0 R>>
endobj

4158 0 obj
<</Title(Scheme 2: Supplier Impersonation and Payment Diversion)/Dest[39 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4157 0 R/Parent 4156 0 R/Next 4159 0 R>>
endobj

4159 0 obj
<</Title(Scheme 3: Salary Diversion and AI-Assisted Impersonation)/Dest[39 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4158 0 R/Parent 4156 0 R/Next 4160 0 R>>
endobj

4160 0 obj
<</Title(Scheme 4: Fabricated Expense Reimbursements)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4159 0 R/Parent 4156 0 R>>
endobj

4161 0 obj
<</Title(DETECTION, RESPONSE AND PROFESSIONAL LESSONS)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/First 4162 0 R/Last 4174 0 R/Count -13/Prev 4156 0 R/Parent 3931 0 R/Next 4178 0 R>>
endobj

4162 0 obj
<</Title(5. Strengthen Identity Verification: As impersonation techniques evolve, organisations should use layered identity checks for sensitive HR and financial processes rather than relying solely on video calls or familiar contact details.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4163 0 R>>
endobj

4163 0 obj
<</Title(6. Encourage Reporting and Follow-Through: Employees should know how to raise concerns, and reports should be assessed promptly and objectively. An investigation should also examine whether weaknesses elsewhere could create similar risks.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4162 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4164 0 R>>
endobj

4164 0 obj
<</Title(The fourth allegation concerned reimbursements for work expenses that had not genuinely occurred.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4163 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4165 0 R>>
endobj

4165 0 obj
<</Title(The DOJ states that the defendants sought reimbursement for a supposed work trip to Las Vegas in December 2025. When photographs were requested as supporting evidence, prosecutors allege that a later trip was organised to create photographs that appeared consistent with the claimed travel period.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4164 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4166 0 R>>
endobj

4166 0 obj
<</Title(This example illustrates why the presence of supporting documents does not automatically establish that an expense is genuine. Photographs, receipts and claim forms must be considered alongside other evidence.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4165 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4167 0 R>>
endobj

4167 0 obj
<</Title(An auditor reviewing travel expenses might compare the claim with travel authorisations, booking records, payment evidence, meeting schedules and the timing of supporting material. Where inconsistencies arise, the appropriate response is further verification.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4166 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4168 0 R>>
endobj

4168 0 obj
<</Title(The Audit Lesson: Evidence should be corroborated. A document may support a claim, but the wider timeline and independent records must also make sense.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4167 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4169 0 R>>
endobj

4169 0 obj
<</Title(What Auditors and Investigators Can Learn)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4168 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4170 0 R>>
endobj

4170 0 obj
<</Title(1. Connect Information Across Departments: Procurement, finance, HR and operations may each hold only part of the relevant information. Comparing records across functions can reveal inconsistencies that individual reviews may miss.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4169 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4171 0 R>>
endobj

4171 0 obj
<</Title(2. Verify Changes Independently: Changes to supplier bank details, employee status, contract quantities and payment instructions should be checked through authorised, independent channels.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4170 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4172 0 R>>
endobj

4172 0 obj
<</Title(3. Examine the Full Transaction Trail: Investigators should establish who initiated a transaction, who approved it, what supporting evidence existed, and where the money ultimately went.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4171 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4173 0 R>>
endobj

4173 0 obj
<</Title(4. Test the Evidence, Not Just its Presence: A signed document, photograph or completed form does not automatically prove that the underlying activity occurred. Dates, sources, and supporting records should be consistent.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4172 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R/Next 4174 0 R>>
endobj

4174 0 obj
<</Title(The Bigger Lesson)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/First 4175 0 R/Last 4177 0 R/Count -3/Prev 4173 0 R/Parent 4161 0 R>>
endobj

4175 0 obj
<</Title(This case illustrates how alleged fraud can exploit the spaces between business processes. The risk becomes clearer when records are checked against independent evidence and against one another.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Parent 4174 0 R/Next 4176 0 R>>
endobj

4176 0 obj
<</Title(For auditors, the objective is not to assume wrongdoing whenever an inconsistency appears. It is to ask the right questions, verify the facts, preserve relevant evidence, and escalate concerns through appropriate procedures.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4175 0 R/Parent 4174 0 R/Next 4177 0 R>>
endobj

4177 0 obj
<</Title(Closing Insight: Effective fraud prevention depends on more than having controls in place. It requires controls that are independently verified, information that is connected across functions, and professionals who are willing to investigate when the evidence does not add up.)/Dest[40 0 R/Fit]/Prev 4176 0 R/Parent 4174 0 R>>
endobj

